From 8cabc61a9daca49f12fbdc514dd83e48f1a96700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Natalia Portillo <claunia@claunia.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:25:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Replace slog with an in-house TRACE/FATAL logger.

The slog upstream repository no longer exists. The library only used
slog_trace/slog_fatal and slog_init, so a small internal logger in
src/log.c replaces it: printf-style, line-atomic output to stderr or to
the file named by AARUFORMAT_LOG_FILE, runtime filtering through
AARUFORMAT_LOG_LEVEL (trace, fatal, none), and lazy one-time
initialization that also covers aaruf_create().

The CMake option is now AARU_ENABLE_LOGGING; USE_SLOG remains as a
deprecated alias. log.h now includes inttypes.h, which several sources
relied on slog.h to provide for PRIu64.
---
 CMakeLists.txt |  36 +++-----
 include/log.h  |  79 ++++++++++++-----
 src/log.c      | 236 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/open.c     |   8 --
 4 files changed, 307 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/log.c

